In Ladybird, a dx or a dy attribute moves the first character its
element renders. Where nested elements start with the same character,
only the attribute of the innermost one applies. Blink resolves the
attributes that way too, in SvgTextLayoutAttributesBuilder::Build().
Gecko does so in SVGTextFrame::ResolvePositionsForNode(), and WebKit in
the resolveCharacterPositioning() of its SVGTextLayoutAlgorithm. The new
test gives the same character positions in Chrome 157.0.8103.79, Firefox
151.0, and WebKit 26.5 as in Ladybird.
